---
/* What this archive rests on.

   The source list used to be seventy lines inline here, which meant it could
   not be counted, checked or added to without editing a page — the same failure
   as the audit and the disputed edges. It is data now: data/sources.tsv.

   Extracting it exposed that the page had gone stale in the worst direction.
   It opened «Almost every source below is an INDEX cited by the family tree,
   not a document this archive has seen», and it closed with a section headed
   «What is not here yet» whose first sentence was «No Italian civil register
   has been read for this family». Both were true on the day the archive was
   built. By the time anyone read them again this archive had opened several
   hundred acts at four comuni and reached the 1720s. A sources page that
   undersells itself is not modesty. */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Sources from "@daviddef/archive-kit/components/Sources.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
import stats from "../data/stats.json";
import sources from "../data/sources.json";

const LABEL = {
  act:   ["read here", "the document itself, read in the original"],
  index: ["index only", "an index entry — it proves a name was written somewhere"],
  tree:  ["the tree", "the family's own compilation"],
  lore:  ["unreferenced", "compiled research with no reference given"],
  wall:  ["a wall", "tried, and it did not answer"],
};
const n = (k) => sources.counts[k] || 0;

/* 21 September 2026. The table became the kit's source rows. The `seen` grade
   did NOT become a group — it cuts across the groups, so it rides on each row
   as a tag, gloss and all. The groups stay exactly as this archive wrote
   them, because "Tried and found wanting" is an argument and not a category.

   Twelve of the twenty-five now link to the thing itself. The thirteen that
   do not are precisely one group — the indexes the family tree cites that
   this archive has never opened — and they are left unlinked on purpose. A
   link would say the collection had been reached, and the group's own
   heading says it has not. */
const groups = sources.groups.map((g) => ({
  label: g.group,
  rows: g.rows.map((r) => ({
    title: r.source,
    tag: LABEL[r.seen][0],
    tagTitle: LABEL[r.seen][1],
    url: r.url,
    what: r.what,
    note: r.note,
    carries: r.usedFor ? "<strong>Used for:</strong> " + r.usedFor : null,
  })),
}));
const reachable = sources.groups.flatMap((g) => g.rows).filter((r) => r.url).length;
---
<Base title="Sources" eyebrow={`${sources.total} sources, ${n("act")} of them read in the original`}
      dek="What this archive rests on — and, for every line of it, whether the document itself has been read or only an index to it.">

  <section class="blk">
    <div class="grid g3">
      <div class="stat"><div class="n">{n("act")}</div><div class="l">read in the original</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="n">{n("index")}</div><div class="l">index only</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="n">{n("wall") + n("lore")}</div><div class="l">walls and hearsay</div></div>
    </div>
    <p class="note" style="margin-top:20px">Read this page with the <a href={u("/method/")}>method</a>
    beside it. <strong>An index entry is a real source and a weak one:</strong> it proves a name was
    written somewhere, and it does not show you the handwriting, the parents, the ages or the address.
    Every row below says which it is. Of the {stats.sources} sources named in the family's own export,
    <strong>only 11 individuals carry a citation at all</strong> — which is why so much of this archive
    is now resting on registers the export never mentioned.</p>
    <p class="note"><strong>{reachable} of the {sources.total} link to the thing itself.</strong> The
    rest are the indexes the tree cites and this archive has never opened — left unlinked on purpose,
    because a link would say they had been reached.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="blk">
    <Sources groups={groups} u={u} html={false} />
  </section>

  <section class="blk" style="border-bottom:0">
    <h2>What is not here yet</h2>
    <div class="prose" style="margin-top:1rem">
      <p>This section used to begin <em>“No Italian civil register has been read for this family. That
      is the largest single gap.”</em> It was true on the day the archive was built and it is kept here,
      struck, because an archive that quietly deletes its own old headline is harder to trust than one
      that shows the correction.</p>
      <p><strong>What is actually missing now is narrower and harder.</strong></p>
      <ul style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:14px;line-height:1.75;color:var(--ink-2);padding-left:20px">
        <li><strong>The parish books of Scilla.</strong> Everything above the 1720s on the Arena side is
        pre-civil. The 1815 marriage bundle names the books and the men who kept them — the
        <em>liber Baptizatorum</em> and <em>liber Defunctorum</em> of the Chiesa Matrice, under archpriest
        D. Giuseppe Ingigneri. The Archdiocese of Reggio Calabria–Bova is the holder, and nothing of it is
        online.</li>
        <li><strong>Piedimonte Etneo after 1893.</strong> Antenati stops there. The marriage of about 1900
        and a death in 1925 sit in the <em>Tribunale</em> duplicate for Catania, which runs to 1929.</li>
        <li><strong>Four files at Brisbane</strong> and <strong>one alien registration file</strong> that
        would state where Maria Nicotra was born. Open access, not digitised, and a copy request rather
        than a search.</li>
        <li><strong>Zambrone's deaths, 1813–1821.</strong> A real hole in the state's copy; the comune's
        own second copy is the only route, and that is a letter.</li>
      </ul>
      <p style="margin-top:14px">Each of those is a row. <a href={u("/worklist/")}>The work list →</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
